#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572778} :activity/id #uuid "f512a6df-58eb-5ba9-9576-bb9ab79c9e12" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049322 :topic/id #uuid "ebecad61-07fb-5ecb-9dcd-758d5fa56d82" :topic/math-academy-id 1810} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572761 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348333 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a498397-bc50-529e-8e10-47f12cf12780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345849} {:answer/id #uuid "4d4f5078-9c9c-5434-884d-abeff808219e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346014} {:answer/id #uuid "516edaf6-39a8-55dd-90e0-7aaeeb8c35e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346050} {:answer/id #uuid "ad405862-61ea-5124-a0de-62ed44cbd68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346862} {:answer/id #uuid "effbbbd2-a34b-5da0-b614-911f26ef50bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347467}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186346014} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dfbae8b-192e-5dbd-a7da-8c84cfb07a0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ee857b14-a370-505a-a029-ad7460463ae5" :question/math-academy-id "q-80117" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,4,-4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $6x-3y+6z=-18.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-3y+6z & =-18 \\\\ 6(1)-3(2)+6z & =-18 \\\\ 6z & =-18 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,2,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,2,-3⟩-⟨5,4,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨6,-3,6⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-4)\\cdot 6+(-2)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 6|}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-24+6+6|}{\\sqrt{36+9+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,-12\\,|}{\\sqrt{81}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4520189c-2f23-58f6-8c5a-da1e7d444ffd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572799}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572778 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315010 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23c37932-b8d1-516f-abf3-f1748834a7af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312239} {:answer/id #uuid "3f3b0406-2681-5fe8-a9d6-e948d2f27a69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{48}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312486} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7e35c1-be2d-55da-bd15-0ac93254cb95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{43}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312817} {:answer/id #uuid "a1272a18-c467-54d3-9f71-ae126c7eade1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313242} {:answer/id #uuid "e1afee6d-ef0d-5bae-8b1d-2c7e13dcdbb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\sqrt{26}}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313752}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312817} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0d43f73-b51f-5e33-b3f5-c33dee8bb5b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "245878e4-0685-5305-b361-ba9fd660a2d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-34074" :question/problem "Given that $Q(2,4,1)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-6,2,9⟩=5$, find the shortest distance from $P(6,-1,0)$ to $Π.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,4,1⟩-⟨6,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-6,2,9⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-4)\\cdot (-6)+5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 9|}{\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{9}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|24+10+9|}{\\sqrt{36+4+81}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|43|}{\\sqrt{121}} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8de1845b-7bd3-5cc9-ac01-91de02bac6f7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572761}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572779 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262941 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "129b0757-3ac6-5753-b6e3-478a8023eb52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260037} {:answer/id #uuid "4de222b6-19ed-5d3c-a87c-f1b937df4849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260536} {:answer/id #uuid "65ac176a-0b06-5588-9781-22d9e0435725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260758} {:answer/id #uuid "816e3b5d-f9fa-5bd9-b29d-3f7e216e3a23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261004} {:answer/id #uuid "df122527-7c53-5616-83fd-4d0c7dd7847e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261846}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260536} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffc75d90-c023-5fb9-a940-576505f511c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0498861d-e4e1-5581-aee5-353d6a78f4f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-129102" :question/problem "Given that $Q(4,-2,8)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-3,6,2⟩=-8$, find the shortest distance from $P(3,-4,2)$ to $Π.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨4,-2,8⟩-⟨3,-4,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,2,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-3,6,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 6+6\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-3+12+12|}{\\sqrt{9+36+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|21|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{7} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9493a861-104a-5833-9f39-6e049c77a66e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572800}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572799 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348336 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00f6631c-af7b-53a2-83af-ac437e78d90b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345363} {:answer/id #uuid "619b3823-d10c-5f60-8462-b61b0c00f5f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346199} {:answer/id #uuid "6b2d9bb2-2fd3-5983-804f-4a5cd3d99900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346278} {:answer/id #uuid "8ddb3ea6-0413-5720-b61a-ab23c633ab83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346583} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb2fcdd-6bc9-502b-bf63-760bd1212667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347459}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345363} :answer-field/id #uuid "9873e119-5653-5fff-9565-620b8e2698f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "32d1647f-476a-5352-bcda-228c154bf2db" :question/math-academy-id "q-80120" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-11,-8,-4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $14x+8y-8z=-6.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=-2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14x+8y-8z & =-6 \\\\ 14(-1)+8(-2)-8z & =-6 \\\\ -8z & =24 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,-2,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,-2,-3⟩-⟨-11,-8,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨10,6,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨14,8,-8⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|10\\cdot 14+6\\cdot 8+1\\cdot (-8)|}{\\sqrt{(14)^{2}+{8}^{2}+(-8)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|140+48-8|}{\\sqrt{196+64+64}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,180\\,|}{\\sqrt{324}} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e3e2ae28-2bca-5084-b4c1-d7fbd0b4a8e2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572779}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572800 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262946 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a1bf0d7-f3ab-56da-9f69-e8fe7acdca78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260643} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa2f25e-eac8-573f-a22c-70c7051fc5ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260945} {:answer/id #uuid "9e90c74b-9340-5886-925a-6fd3dc9f6d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261250} {:answer/id #uuid "b2e32ad6-74af-5732-bdfa-a17a20a619ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261455} {:answer/id #uuid "fac998bb-1203-5d71-bc3a-98304a447645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262068}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260945} :answer-field/id #uuid "7eac6dd3-6114-5470-be8e-c3ff6f56e4f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7213d75b-15a3-5beb-aba1-e3068433b4a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-129120" :question/problem "Given that $Q(5,-1,9)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨3,-6,-2⟩=3$, find the shortest distance from $P(7,-2,8)$ to $Π.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨5,-1,9⟩-⟨7,-2,8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨3,-6,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-2)\\cdot 3+1\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6-6-2|}{\\sqrt{9+36+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-14|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{7} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e7731aae-63ac-5bf9-97b3-13fce07182f4"}] :activity/title "The Shortest Distance Between a Plane and a Point" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572317}]}
